<!-- Worked example: a zero-failures criterion beside an inferential one.

     well-formed is a compliance criterion: POLICY requirement 0.95,
     alpha 0.05, 200 samples, k_min = 196 under compliance/exact-binomial;
     196 of 200 passed, so it PASSes. no-harmful-advice is observational:
     no failure in 200 trials, so it PASSes too, by observation alone.

     <statistics> describes the inferential criterion only (Statistical
     Companion §1.4.5, §10.2): standard error and Wilson lower bound of
     196/200, and its requirement 0.95. The observational row states its
     mode and its counts, nothing else.
     The sizing entries come from the inferential criterion's design.
     <verdict> names no rule, because no single rule decided every
     criterion: one was decided by observation. -->
